# [K49] (docs/dev/known_issues.md), found 2026-09-05 by lane utfprom while
# promoting the D27 blinded utf8 corpus (tests/utf8/) against the
# just-merged [M5.0] stage 2 tree. Moved from
# tests/utf8/axis09_nextpos_findall.rxt's "midstart-row3-boundary" block —
# see that file's own pointer comment at the block's former position.
#
# `(?<!.)` at startpos=2 over a subject whose byte 2 is a real UTF-8
# CHARACTER BOUNDARY (alpha ends there, beta begins) is ARGUED by the D27
# extract (Sec 2.6.1.1's mid-character-startpos table) to answer NO MATCH:
# the assertion is false at position 2 (alpha precedes it), and an
# unanchored retry from there must only ever try LATER CHARACTER
# BOUNDARIES — the next of which is position 4 (subject end), where the
# assertion is false again (beta precedes it). No PCRE2 oracle produces
# this cell directly; `pcrec-ARGUED` is this project's own design position,
# not a measured libpcre2 answer.
#
# pcrec's LIVE answer today is a MATCH at (3,3) — byte offset 3 sits
# INSIDE beta's own two-byte encoding, not a character boundary at all.
# Kept HERE, pinning the ARGUED/correct expectation (not pcrec's current
# answer), per this directory's own convention: "the cells stay, they stay
# loud, and if pcrec is ever changed to reproduce it this file FIRES."

# pcre2-only (byte-vs-utf8 subject-decode mismatch in the default python
# oracle — see tests/utf8/CLAUDE.md; not a python-verifiability question
# about the CONSTRUCT itself)
pattern (?<!.)
encoding utf8
features lookaround
ns 2 "\xce\xb1\xce\xb2"
